My take on the table in the link I cited - When I want a
specific numerical luck I want to know exact methods
to change it not random ones.  As the "first" clover at
an altar gives a random number that can't be depended
on to know my number is 1.  This "first" is in the sense
of moving from 0 to positive not the actual first.

Because of the random boast going up from 0, I tend
to max out to 13 then use fixed methods to get down
to my desired number.  I have a detailed write-up on
why I want exact luck numbers at altars if you would like.
It got included in a spoiler a couple of years ago but I
haven't seen it included in Eva Myers compilation yet.


